## Context
Three residual gaps left by merged reading-2 tickets. Tracker:
`tickets/0578-reading-2-wave-tracking-ticket.erg`.
Reading-2 findings 15, 2 (residual), and 16 (residual).

## Findings

### Finding 15 — Annex C intro repeats the caption
Annex C (`sec:annex-recognition`) intro restated the figure's
"plants as rows, runs as columns, grouped by status then capacity,
blue = recognised" layout almost verbatim with the figure caption.
Shorten the intro so it only carries what the caption does NOT say:
the contrast with `fig:direct-base` (counts vs. which plants are
missed) and the forward pointer to `tbl:status-difficulty`.

### Finding 2 (residual) — Annex B agents table column width
The Annex B agents table (`sec:annex-exp2`) Surface column used a
single hard-coded `p{0.48\linewidth}` fraction while the other three
were auto `l`. Make the column widths automatic/balanced. Switching
to `tabularx` with an auto-sizing `X` column for Surface removes the
hard-coded fraction and lets LaTeX fill the remaining width.

### Finding 16 (residual) — recognition-rate column header
The §7.1 prose + caption (`tbl:status-difficulty`) were reworded to
"the average probability of a plant being found by an Experiment 1
model run", but the generated EN table column header still read
"Recognition rate". Fix the EMITTER
(`src/aedist/tabulate_status_difficulty.py`, English function), not
the artifact; regenerate `tab_status_difficulty_en.tex` via the make
target and commit it. New header: "Avg. detection prob." The French
table (`format_status_latex`) keeps "Taux de reconnaissance" — its
French caption matches it; this finding is EN-only.

